    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0442" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.156/91</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dickson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 164</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Pursuant to a request contained in a letter
                    dated August 12, 1920,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d397-f1"/> from the Asunción Port
                    Concession Corporation of 44 Cedar Street, New York City, there are transmitted
                    herewith for your information and for such use as in your discretion you may see
                    fit <pb facs="0443" n="343" xml:id="pg343"/> to make of them, copies of a letter
                    dated August 11th<anchor n="21" xml:id="d397-f2"/> from that corporation
                    announcing its creation, and copies of the enclosures thereto, which are a
                    certificate of incorporation of the Asuncion Port Concession Corporation and
                    certain authenticating documents.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d397-f3"/> Pursuant to
                    the same request, there is also transmitted a copy of a letter dated August
                        11th<anchor n="21" xml:id="d397-f4"/> from the Construction and Engineering
                    Finance Company, Equitable Building, New York City, announcing that that company
                    and MacArthur Brothers have joined their interests with the Asuncion Port
                    Concession Corporation.</p>
                <p>The reason given by the new corporation for asking that these documents be
                    transmitted to you is that you may be in a position intelligently to deal with
                    any matter that may arise in connection therewith.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A.
                            Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
